     "explanation": "Among 10,000 people: ~1 has the disease (and will likely test positive); the other 9,999 are healthy, of whom ~500 will get false positives. So ~501 total positive tests, only ~1 real → roughly **0.2% probability**. This is **base rate neglect** writ large. The test's 99% sensitivity number is psychologically dominating; the 1-in-10,000 base rate is mathematically dominating. The math wins.",
