     "explanation": "Asch's most important follow-up finding: a single dissenter — even one who gave a *different wrong* answer — collapsed conformity rates from ~37% to under 10%. Humans only need 'one other person sees what I see' to resist crowd pressure. This is why the courage to be the first dissenter matters disproportionately: you're not just expressing your view, you're creating cover for everyone else who had doubts.",
