     "question": "A city has spent forty million dollars on a half-built light-rail line that ridership studies now suggest will never recoup its operating costs. The city council votes to spend another fifteen million dollars to finish it, arguing that stopping now would waste the forty million already spent. Which bias is most directly on display, and why is the reasoning flawed?",
